-- title:
--   Original ruin-stopped chronological Stieltjes timing yields source HJB expected dividend budget
-- statement:
--   For the original spectrally negative Levy process, admissible left-continuous dividends and right-continuous ruin-stopped bounded time, assume the exact stopped source subsequence limit and mean-sign hypotheses already exposed by the accepted source HJB consumer. Instead of assuming its eventual dividend residual inequality, require a directly source-defined timing functional, a.e. compact-local-band control, and the chronological Chat05 residual upper bounded by H plus that timing error. The accepted cofinal timing absorption proves the missing eventual residual premise; then accepted original payment-only HJB consumer yields integrable cash, real terminal/cash expectation budget and nested ENNReal dividend upper bound. This does not silently prove the mixed Gaussian jump source limit or chronological signed Stieltjes inequality.
-- source:
--   Avram Proposition 4(i), Eq. (5.11)-(5.13); accepted 088497d3 and conditional cofinal residual 06 source alignment

